-- title:
--   q-expansion field of Γ_H(N)∩Γ₀(Nℓ) generated by j(q^ℓ)
-- statement:
--   Let $K$ be a field, $N \ge 1$ a natural number, $\ell$ a prime, and suppose $N\ell \ne 0$ in $K$ and $\ell \nmid N$; let $H$ be a subgroup of $(\mathbb{Z}/N)^\times$. Here $\Gamma_H(N)$ denotes the subgroup [`CohCarrier.GammaH N H`](def/CohCarrier_Level.html#L133) of $\mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb{Z})$, namely the image in $\mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb{Z})$ of those $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(N)$ whose lower-right entry, read as a unit of $\mathbb{Z}/N$, lies in $H$; for a subgroup $\Gamma \le \mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb{Z})$, [`ModularCurve.qExpFunctionFieldC K Γ`](def/ModularCurve_X1.html#L101) is the intermediate field of $K((q))$ generated over $K$ by all quotients $\overline{p_f}/\overline{p_g}$ of reductions to $K$ of integral $q$-expansions $p_f, p_g$ of modular forms $f, g$ of one and the same weight $k$ on $\Gamma$ (regarded inside $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{R})$), with $\overline{p_g} \ne 0$; [`ModularCurve.jqModC K`](def/ModularCurve_JqCoeff.html#L15) is $q^{-1}$ times the reduction to $K$ of the power series $E_4^3 \cdot \eta^{-24}$-type numerator `jNum`, i.e. the $q$-expansion of $j$ over $K$; and [`ModularCurve.qExpand K ℓ`](def/ModularCurve_X0.html#L25) is the ring homomorphism of $K((q))$ substituting $q \mapsto q^\ell$ (multiplying all exponents by $\ell$). The assertion is the equality of intermediate fields $$\bar F(\Gamma_H(N)) \vee K\big(j(q^\ell)\big) = \bar F\big(\Gamma_H(N) \cap \Gamma_0(N\ell)\big)$$ inside $K((q))$.
--
--   This is the statement that, in every characteristic prime to $N\ell$, the $q$-expansion function field of level $\Gamma_H(N) \cap \Gamma_0(N\ell)$ is obtained from that of $\Gamma_H(N)$ by adjoining $j(q^\ell)$, equivalently that the modular equation $\Phi_\ell(j, Y)$ remains irreducible over the level-$N$ function field. It is used in the construction of polynomial relations for the degeneracy/Hecke correspondence at $\ell$, being cited by the results producing a polynomial over the $\Gamma_0$-field whose evaluation realises the inclusion of the $\ell$-level field.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_qExpFunctionFieldC_gammaH_sup_adjoin_qExpand_jqModC_eq_qExpFunctionFieldC_gammaH_inf_gamma0_of_not_dvd.lean

